CM_ SG_ 110 MATURITY_398_CANDIDATE_RAW "Radar firmware: one 7-bit field; not read. Values above 15 on 9.2% of frames. Counts down from about 6 to 1 as a track matures. Adds no velocity-error or survival information once track age is known.";
CM_ SG_ 110 FIELD_405_RAW "Not read by the radar firmware. Raw 49 on 82% of frames. Meaning unknown.";
CM_ SG_ 110 AZIMUTH_CENTER_RAW "Radar firmware: 0.00025*raw-1.02375 (zero at 4095), valid below 8192; unlike the edges, the radar does not pass it through atan here. Positive left. Equals the midpoint of the two edge fields on 97-99.9% of observations, so it is the same quantity as the edges: a tangent. The earlier 2^-12 rad per count, zero 4096, was 2.4% small.";
CM_ SG_ 110 AZIMUTH_EDGE_A_RAW "Left angular edge; same encoding as AZIMUTH_CENTER. The radar firmware passes it through atan, so it is the tangent of the angle: tan +-1.024 is about +-45.7 deg. Always at or left of the center. Clips at 8191.";
