CM_ SG_ 114 FIELD_344_RAW "Radar firmware: 0.002*raw-10, valid below 8001 (+-10). Raw 5000 (0) on 68% of frames. Not acceleration: on lead-like objects its 90th-percentile magnitude is 0.04-0.12 against 0.55-1.83 m/s^2 of lead acceleration, r <= 0.2 (docs/object-length-217.md). Meaning unknown.";
CM_ SG_ 114 FIELD_360_RAW "Not read by the A230 radar firmware; the MY22 firmware (A070) defines 362:6 here instead. Median raw 48. Meaning unknown.";
CM_ SG_ 114 FIELD_368_RAW "Radar firmware: 0.0025*raw, valid below 1024. Raw 1 on 64% of frames. Meaning unknown.";
CM_ SG_ 114 AUX2_378_CANDIDATE_RAW "Radar firmware: same encoding as the azimuth fields, 0.00025*raw-1.02375, valid below 8192 (initial value 4095), and the radar passes it through atan like the edges: a tangent. Not signed 13-bit: with this decode its sign matches the azimuth on 98-99% of populated frames (routes 171, 17b, 19d), against 1-2% for a signed read. Shares one subrecord with ANGULAR_WIDTH_480: both hold their defaults together (8190 here; bits 480-487 zero) on about two thirds of observations. The MY22 firmware has no getter for it.";
