CM_ SG_ 122 REL_VELOCITY_UNCERTAINTY_RAW "Bosch A REL_VELOCITY_UNCERTAINTY counterpart (accepted, raw units): velocity-noise specific and monotonic with empirical vRel noise on ten recordings. Radar firmware: 0.1*raw, valid below 1024, unit unnamed. Nonlinear against our measured vRel noise (the adapter maps it empirically).";
CM_ SG_ 122 UNCERTAINTY_160_CANDIDATE_RAW "Radar firmware: 10 bits, 0.02*raw, valid below 1024. Mostly 1-2; higher on young and laterally offset objects. Weak noise association. Unit unnamed.";
CM_ SG_ 122 ACQUISITION_186_CANDIDATE_RAW "Radar firmware: 6 bits, 0.01*raw, valid below 64. Starts near 23 on newborn tracks and decays to about 2. Carries little information beyond track age.";
CM_ SG_ 122 UNCERTAINTY_192_CANDIDATE_RAW "Radar firmware: 9 bits, 0.1*raw, valid below 512. Decays with age; mixed velocity and lateral noise association, not specific to one noise. Unit unnamed.";
